TITLE      Proton polarization in gamma He3,4 -> xp reactions and M0233  1    3 
            quasideuteron model.                                  M0233  1    4 
AUTHOR     (A.A.Zybalov,S.P.Karasev,O.G.Konovalov,S.V.Marekhin,   M0233  1    5 
            P.V.Sorokin,Yu.O.Storozhenko,A.E.Tenishev)            M0233  1    6 
INSTITUTE  (4UKRKFT)                                              M0233  1    7 
REFERENCE  (J,YF,47,1505,1988)                                    M0233  1    8 
           (J,SNP,47,955,1988) - Eng.trans.of YF,47,1505,1988     M0233  1    9 
FACILITY   (LINAC,4UKRKFT). It was 2 GeV accelerator LUE-2.       M0233  1   10 
INC-SOURCE (BRST) With end-point energy 600 MeV.                  M0233  1   11 
INC-SPECT  The size of the photon beam was made as 16*16 mm-sq.   M0233  1   12 
METHOD     (EXTB,SITA). The inclusive proton polarisation in      M0233  1   13 
           photon interaction with He-3 and He-4 nuclei was       M0233  1   14 
           produced.                                              M0233  1   15 
DETECTOR   (IOCH)                                                 M0233  1   16 
PART-DET   (P)                                                    M0233  1   17 
SAMPLE     The liquid target with 120 mm in a long and 25 mm      M0233  1   18 
           in a diameter was used.                                M0233  1   19 
ANALYSIS   The polarization was independent from the minimum angleM0233  1   20 
           of the secondary protons scattering on the He-3 and    M0233  1   21 
           He-4 nuclei. As the result of the analysis the angle ofM0233  1   22 
           polarization was taken to equal 5. degrees.            M0233  1   23 
ADD-RES    (COMP). Comparison with polarization values measured   M0233  1   24 
           in the Gd - pn reaction under similar conditions.      M0233  1   25 
ERR-ANALYS (ERR-S) Statistical errors are presented.              M0233  1   26 
           Distribution of pi-mesons was less than 2%.            M0233  1   27 
           Distribution of protons from a target wall was         M0233  1   28 
           less than 65%.                                         M0233  1   29 
COMMENT    Ang-min is the minimum value of scattering angle.      M0233  1   30 
           Ang-max is the maximum value of scattering angle.      M0233  1   31 
